@startuml user_telemetry_dashboard_classes
title User telemetry dashboard -- self-validating cache (no lifecycle coupling, no new columns)
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

' STRATEGY
'  Historical (terminal renders) is immutable -> compute via a FEW indexed
'  GROUP BY queries, cache the blob in Redis per user WITH a cheap freshness
'  marker (terminal count + MAX(completed_at)).  Each read re-reads the
'  marker (one small query, shared with the live query); cache reused while
'  the marker is unchanged, recomputed only when a render completes/deletes.
'  ALL Redis access is in the service, on the read path -- the render
'  lifecycle is NOT involved.  No denormalized columns: engine comes from
'  resolved_scene_json via Postgres ``#>>``.

package "serverV2/users" {
  class "user_profile_repository.py\nUserProfileRepository" as UPR <<existing>>
  class "user_telemetry_repository.py\nUserTelemetryRepository" as UTR <<new, sibling of UPR>> {
    + historical(user_id)   -- few GROUP BY (status, engine#>>, month, fleet/gpu+gpu_seconds)
    + marker_and_live(user_id) -- 1 small query: terminal {count, max_completed}
                                  + active renders live aggregate
    + insights(user_id)     -- render_telemetry: top gpu, avg vram, blender, denoiser
  }

  package "users/telemetry" <<new submodule>> {
    class UserTelemetryService <<new>> {
      + get(user_id) : TelemetryDTO
      .. read path (owns ALL redis access) ..
      1 marker_and_live(uid)
      2 redis.get; marker match? reuse : recompute historical + redis.set
      3 merge historical + live -> DTO
    }
  }
}

package "serverV2/api/routers" {
  class "users.py :: GET /me/telemetry" as ROUTER <<edit>> {
    auth -> service.get(user.uid)
  }
}

package "serverV2/infrastructure" {
  class RedisClient <<reuse>> {
    telemetry:{env}:{uid} = {aggregate, marker}
    no TTL -- self-validated by marker
  }
}

ROUTER --> UserTelemetryService
UserTelemetryService --> UTR : historical / marker_and_live / insights
UserTelemetryService --> RedisClient : get + (re)set on marker change

package "desktop -- frontend (recharts)" {
  class "TelemetryPage.jsx" as PAGE <<new>>
  class useUserTelemetry <<new, hook>> {
    fetch on visit; poll ~10s only while active renders exist
  }
  class "api.getUserTelemetry" as API <<new>>
  class "components/telemetry/*" as COMP <<new>> {
    StatCard, FleetDonut, GpuBar, EngineDonut,
    RendersOverTimeArea, StatusDonut, FunFactsPanel
    -- derive footage / % / biggest-render here (display only)
  }
  class "Sidebar RENTEE_PAGES" as NAV <<edit>> {
    + {id: telemetry, label: "Stats"}
  }
}

PAGE --> useUserTelemetry
useUserTelemetry --> API
API --> ROUTER
PAGE --> COMP
NAV ..> PAGE

note bottom of UserTelemetryService
  No invalidator, no lifecycle step.  "Invalidation" is implicit:
  a completed/deleted render changes (count, MAX(completed_at)),
  so the NEXT read sees a marker mismatch and recomputes + re-caches.
  Heavy aggregate runs only after the terminal set changes; steady
  state = 1 small marker+live query per read (cache hit otherwise).
end note

note bottom of UTR
  Inclusive base (ALL fleets): render_groups + jobs + output_frames.
  engine = resolved_scene_json::jsonb #>> '{heaviness,render_engine}'
           (GROUP BY the extracted value -- NO new column).
  render_telemetry = enrichment only (success + non-community) ->
  clearly-labeled "Render insights" section.
end note
@enduml
